# **Webhooks**

Webhooks let external applications receive real-time notifications when events occur in Taskip.&nbsp;

Instead of repeatedly checking for updates, your system automatically receives HTTP callbacks whenever subscribed events are triggered.

### **Navigation Path**

Settings → Webhook

![](./webhooks/content/image-114.png)

### **Creating a Webhook**

1. Go to Settings and open Webhook.
1. Click + Add New Webhook.

![](./webhooks/content/image-110-1024x311.png)

1. Enter a Webhook Name to identify the integration\
   *(e.g., “CRM Contact Sync”)*.
1. Paste your Webhook URL — the endpoint that will receive event data.
1. Select an HTTP Method:
   - POST — Sends event data in the request body *(recommended)*
   - GET — Sends event data as URL parameters

![](./webhooks/content/image-112.png)

1. Add Custom Headers by clicking + Add Header (Optional)\
   *(useful for authentication tokens)*.

![](./webhooks/content/image-109.png)

1. Select the Events to Subscribe to by choosing one or more categories:
   - Support — Support ticket events
   - Form — Form submission events
   - Sales — Sales pipeline events
   - Company — Workspace and company events
   - Contact — Contact creation and updates
   - Document — Document-related events
   - Quotation — Quotation events
   - Invoice — Invoice events
   - Meeting — Meeting and booking events
   - Project — Project and task events

Using the dropdown menu to select sections:

![](./webhooks/content/image-111.png)

8. Click Save Webhook to activate the webhook.

![](./webhooks/content/image-113.png)

### **Testing Your Webhook**

- Trigger an event in Taskip related to the subscribed category
- Check your receiving application’s logs to confirm the webhook payload is received and parsed correctly.

{% table %}
---
- **Tips**\
  \* Use tools like **RequestBin** or **Webhook. site** to inspect webhook payloads during development\
  \* Secure your endpoint by validating headers or signatures\
  \* Subscribe only to required events to reduce unnecessary traffic
{% /table %}
